WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.635 line:0%
-♪ You can let it
wreck your day ♪

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.370 line:0%
♪ You can pray that
it goes away ♪

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.908 line:0%
♪ Or let something wild and
wonderful break through ♪

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:13.179 line:0%
♪ We're ripping up
the recipe ♪

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:17.550
♪ Let go of how it has to be ♪

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.919
♪ You know you can't
plan it in advance ♪

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.154
♪ Gotta lose yourself
in the dance ♪

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:26.126
♪ It's perfect unexpectedly ♪

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.726
-Mom?

00:00:27.726 --> 00:00:30.163
-♪ when you rip up the recipe ♪

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.498
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Constance Wu!

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.568
That was a clip from her new
movie, "Lyle, Lyle, Crocodile."

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.671
And you were just telling me,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.172
that is a real crocodile.

00:00:40.172 --> 00:00:42.475
That is not...

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.777
-Mm-hmm.
-That was really good.

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.177
-Yep.

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:47.847
-You must have had a lot of
faith in the trainer on set.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.316
-Well, I actually wanted to
play the crocodile,

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.485
but then they said, "No,
we're having the real thing."

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.754
-Well, this is
your current headshot.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.655
-Yeah.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:58.824
-So this is very exciting,
to do --

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:00.960
I would imagine doing
a family film like this

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.096
is more exciting when you
yourself have a family.

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:05.965
One of the differences since
the last time we saw you,

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.634
you have a two-year-old.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.702
Congratulations.
-I had a baby.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.539
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. Thank you.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.174
-Now, will she be able to watch?

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.010
Will you show her this film, or
is she still a little too young?

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.979
-I feel like I'm gonna just
go straight to "Hustlers."

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.314
-Yeah, I think "Hustlers."
-Show her that.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.049
Show her the good career path.
This is the real me.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:27.853
-This is a movie about
making money.

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:29.122
-[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:32.091
Well, I mean, I will --
I don't care.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.926
She can watch "Hustlers,"
but not now.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.361
She can't even sit still
for more than, like, 5 minutes.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.662
-Yeah, that's the thing.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:38.064
It's not really about
whether they're appropriate.

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.399
They just have no interest.
-Yeah.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.434
She's just, like, running around
all over the place.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.869
But she loves animal,
so, you know?

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:45.338
-I think eventually,
this is gonna be a hit.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.672
-I hope so.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.641
-I wondered,
because we still have

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:51.410
our pet dog that we had
before we had kids.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:56.082
I don't feel proud of this,
but we do pay less attention

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:57.450
to our dog
now that we have children.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.252
Do you still have your rabbit?

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.888
-I don't even remember.
I've completely abandoned her.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.089
Just kidding. Just kidding.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.223
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.659
No, this is a recent picture.
-Oh, good.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:07.927
So she's still with you.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.328
She's like
a little, old lady now.

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:10.596
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.731
-What's her name again?
-Her name is Lida Rose.

00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:13.766
-Lida Rose?
-Yeah.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.301
-That's a beautiful name.
-Thank you.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:18.170
-A little much for a rabbit.
-Not for her.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.338
-Okay, gotcha.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.074
-Now, you mentioned that
she's sort of

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:22.808
a grand dame now of rabbits.

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:24.810
And you think
she looks like someone.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.180
-Yes, well, last time
we were on here,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.348
I was like,
"She resembles Jeremy Irons."

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.317
-You did say that.
-But now that she's aged...

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.619
-She's aged out of Jeremy Irons.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:36.889
-I really, truly think
she looks like --

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:40.326
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:43.263
-It does look like Maggie.
It's a dowager countess look.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:46.165
-It is. I've just got to put a
hat on her and she's there.

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.767
-[ Laughter ]
-You know?

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.101
-It's really quite something.

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:51.904
Does your daughter have
any interest in the rabbit?

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:54.707
-For about a minute.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.575
The way she has interest in
everything for about a minute.

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:57.910
-Gotcha.
-But yeah.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.979
-Does the rabbit tense up
when the baby comes around?

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.982
'Cause our dog has not warmed up
to our young err children.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.117
-My rabbit, if you pet her
on the head --

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.518
she loves being pet, like,
right here --

00:03:06.518 --> 00:03:08.888
she doesn't care, she loves you.
-Oh, great.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.622
-And then if you don't,
she's just like,

00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:12.892
"I don't care about you,"
and she just goes away.

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.727
-Well, you know what?
She knows what she likes.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:15.861
-She knows what she wants, yep.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.664
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.898
I really appreciate you
making the time,

00:03:19.898 --> 00:03:21.100
sharing your stories,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.401
and it's always such a pleasure
to see you.

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:23.569
-Thank you.
-Congrats on your movie.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.003
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.003 --> 00:03:26.238
-Constance Wu, everybody.

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:28.574
"Lyle, Lyle, Crocodile" is
in theaters this Friday.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.843
"Making a Scene," right here,

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.879
is on sale now
wherever books are sold.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.480
Please support local
and independent bookstores.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.748
We'll be right back
with Ramy Youssef.

